  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday morning through next Saturday)\nIssued at 212 PM EST Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nThe long term starts off with another system as a low pressure \ncenter moves through the Great Lakes, brining a cold front across \nmuch of the southeast. Rainfall values between half and one and a \nhalf inch are expected across the CWA beginning Wednesday evening \nand running through Saturday afternoon. A few thunderstorms are \npossible, as temps climb into the mid 70s on Wednesday, but \nwidespread severe weather is not expected at this time as much of \nthe stronger dynamics to this system will be off to the north and \nwest. \n\nAfter the front moves through, afternoon high temperatures will \ncontinue to stay above normal as building high pressure from the \ngulf pushes warm tropical air into the region. With highs in the low \nto mid 70s and overnight lows in the 40s and 50s, temperatures will \nbe running anywhere from 5-10 degrees above normal for early \nNovember.",
